Package: presence-streamer
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: ProdBytes <julio@nu01.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: video
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/prodbytes/presence
Depends: adduser, ffmpeg (>= 7:5.1), rclone, python3, python3-opencv, python3-numpy
Recommends: rpicam-apps | libcamera-apps
Description: Presence streamer: a Raspberry Pi camera for a Presence profile
 Records the camera continuously (hardware H.264 where the Pi has an
 encoder), in chunks, and uploads each one, sealed, to a premium Presence
 profile's cloud folder with rclone. Chunks with a person or an animal in
 them (YOLOv4-tiny, OpenCV) become events in the profile, as a phone's
 motion clips; the rest are deleted.
 .
 Set it up with: sudo presence-streamer setup
 (asks for the profile ID and a Google sign-in, then starts
 presence-streamer.service, which runs at every boot).
 Settings: /etc/default/presence-streamer.
